feat(ui): iOS Day and iOS Night palettes as the default themes

DESIGN_SPEC section 1. Adds two built-in themes and makes them the
defaults on first launch. Saved theme choices of existing installs are
kept, and all upstream themes stay available in the theme picker.

- ios_day.attheme: a copy of upstream bluebubbles.attheme (Blue theme)
  with the iOS Classic colors appended: grouped background #EFEFF4, white
  cells, #C8C7CC separators, #0088FF accent, #E1FFC7 and #FFFFFF bubbles,
  chat list, input panel and nav bar colors.
- ios_night.attheme: a copy of upstream night.attheme with the iOS Night
  colors appended: black background, #1C1C1D cells, #1D1D1D incoming
  bubbles, #61BCF9 to #0088FF outgoing gradient, chat list and nav bar.
- Theme.java: registers both themes after the upstream ones, makes them
  the default day and night themes, and marks them light and dark by name,
  so isDark() does not need a theme file path (built-in themes have none).

Later keys in a theme file override earlier ones, so the appended iOS
values win over the upstream base values.

Deviations (listed in PROGRESS.md): the chat background is a solid color
(#A2D7F5 / #000000) instead of the iOS pattern wallpaper. iOS Night keeps
Android's accent for buttons and links, because iOS uses white there and
Android draws white text on accent buttons in many places.
